# fork/verify/known-failing — upstream tests that legitimately go red under the
# fork's seams (series commits telemetry-analytics-off, telemetry-feedback-off,
# telemetry-statsig-strip, telemetry-defaults-none).
#
# Format: one nextest filterset expression per line ('#' comments, blank lines
# ignored).  Consumers OR the expressions together, e.g. to exclude them from
# the required-green set:
#   cargo nextest run -E "not ($(grep -v '^#' known-failing | grep . | paste -sd'|' - | sed 's/|/ or /g'))"
#
# Provenance: the telemetry-seam verification pass, then re-derived
# test-by-test against
# the rust-v0.149.0 tree by the seam commit itself, which seeded this file;
# each later series commit adds its own cause group.
# Three causes:
#   (1) analytics force-off — `Config.analytics_enabled` is `Some(false)` for
#       every config layer, so `AnalyticsEventsClient` never builds a queue and
#       every test awaiting a POST to /codex/analytics-events/events times out;
#   (2) accepted Caveat A — `otel_init.rs` nulls the WHOLE metrics exporter
#       when analytics is off, user BYO OTLP collectors included, so tests that
#       await their own /metrics endpoint time out;
#   (3) feedback force-off — `Config.feedback_enabled` is `false`, so the
#       `/feedback` TUI command and the `feedback/upload` RPC report disabled.
#
# NOT in this list, deliberately (verified to keep passing):
# * mcp-server lib.rs default-analytics assertions and app-server
#   v2/analytics.rs :56/:81 — they assert an untouched constant or reset
#   `analytics_enabled` themselves after load;
# * cli clap flag tests — parsing only;
# * otel crate unit/suite tests — they build `OtelSettings` directly with
#   explicit exporters, and `resolve_exporter(Statsig)` already returned None
#   under debug_assertions before the strip;
# * app-server v2/remote_control.rs — passes `default_analytics_enabled` to the
#   spawn helper but never awaits an analytics POST;
# * app-server v2/turn_steer.rs `turn_steer_rejects_oversized_text_input` and
#   `turn_steer_rejects_context_only_input_without_merging_context` — they
#   mount the analytics capture server but never await it;
# * core config_tests.rs `metrics_exporter_defaults_to_*` — the seam commit
#   flips that expectation in place (the one upstream test it edits);
# * app-server v2/curated_mcp_sync.rs
#   `existing_thread_loads_api_curated_mcp_after_auth_switch_sync` — its
#   fixture opts back in via ORE_CURATED_PLUGINS_REPO, so the sync clones the
#   local git fixture exactly as upstream's hard-coded repo did.

# --- (3) feedback force-off -------------------------------------------------
# Passes `-c analytics.enabled=true` and expects three or more POSTs to
# /events; the seam pins analytics_enabled to Some(false), so no queue is built
# and nothing is ever sent. This is the behaviour codex-fork-invariants asserts.
package(codex-exec) & test(shutdown_flushes_completed_turn_and_file_diff)
# Asserts `feedback_enabled == true` for a default `[feedback]` table.
package(codex-core) & test(feedback_enabled_defaults_to_true)
